{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals","id":18885,"title":"Mummy and Magical Items from other Supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-26T19:28:12-08:00","id":18885,"title":"Mummy and Magical Items from other Supernaturals","content":"I've been asking for this since the Preview Edition of the Core, but I would like one of the books to answer how Mummies interact with other Supernatural Items. I know some just don't want to handle anything nonMummy in their games, good for them but I am one who would like some answers for these. The major purpose of the Arisen after all was to collect Items of Power and bring them to the Judges. Relics aren't only for Mummies, they were originally supposed to be the general misc. Supernatural Item of the NWOD, Aegis Kai Doru are dedicated to them as well (though some implication is that they call all Supernatural Items Relics). Tokens mechanically are very similar to Relics, only with a different Origin. OF all the Items Tokens and Relics are mechanically the most similar. The reason why Relics are gathered is still a mystery, but we have a good indication that its mostly because of their nature as Vessels for Sekhem. But Perhaps Some Supernal Artifacts possessed by Mages would also be worthy of collection.<br /> <br /> I think this would be worthy of at least a sidebar in one of the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T19:42:47-08:00","id":18891,"title":"","content":"Given the associations of Sekhem with memory imprinting, life, death and permanence, I would expect other magical items may not necessarily be of the same interest to the Judges of Duat, but I would be very interested to see what the Arisen would do about discovering a Sin-Eater mystery cult with memorabilia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T19:46:38-08:00","id":18894,"title":"","content":"Sekhem might not be a mutually exclusive trait, perhaps its a quality that can be found in things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T20:13:23-08:00","id":18904,"title":"","content":"I too would like an official answer at least as a sidebar, but I'll just throw out some ideas for house-ruling.<br /> <br /> 1&gt; For my purposes, any AKD &quot;Relics&quot; are interchangeably Risen &quot;Relics&quot; as well. I mean, all the AKD stuff has drawbacks of some sort, which aren't QUITE curses, but could be seen to be similar. I would allow Mummies to treat them as Mummy relics with a dot value equal to their Hunter Merit dot value. Likewise, I would allow (foolish) AKD Hunters to retain captured Mummy relics as AKD Merit relics at a dot cost equal to their mummy relic rating. If that made sense.<br /> <br /> 1B&gt; Since they kind of GAVE us WoD Reliquary as a bonus PDF with some of the pledge level for the Kickstarter, one ASSUMES that the devs intend that we should be able to use Reliquary Relics as, at least, building blocks for Mummy game relics. Basically, with Reliquary system relics you just have to judge what dot rating you want to give the item (since they don't really seem to have ratings as such) just in case your players want to eat their new toy instead of returning it to Duat.<br /> <br /> 2&gt; PERSONALLY, I see Geist and Mummy sharing the themes of life, death, unlife, and the underworld pretty closely. I would rule that Geist mementos and Mummy relics are different things, but share an energy. So, I'd let a Mummy drain a lesser memento for pillars, and Greater items (like Death Masks) might yield Sekhem. Similarly, I would allow a Sin-Eater to destroy a Relic and gain the plasm/healing benefit he'd get from sacrificing a Memento.<br /> <br /> 3&gt; Likewise, I would say that, since Sekhem is the power of eternal life/the underworld Duat, that Mage Imbued items or Artifacts that are tied to EITHER the Life or Death spheres would have an energy that resonates with/can be pulled out as Sekhem. Likewise, a Mage with an interest in either sphere might find a Risen Relic, &quot;Interesting&quot;, to say the least. Perhaps if one were to study some we might learn a little more about who and what the Shaniatu really were... <br /> <br /> 4&gt; Prometheans don't seem to have any sort of magic items (other than Vitriol) and I don't see Changeling magic really &quot;Meshing&quot; with Mummy magic, so I'd just rule them as seperate. No real interactions going on there. Same for Vampires, No magic items that I know of.<br /> <br /> 5&gt; Werewolves magic items are, I believe, powered by Spirits, and spirits and ghosts are different, so unless a Fetish is powered by a spirit that would for some reason have a real resonance with the underworld or the mummies Deathless state, I doubt the Risen would even register the item's magic even if they handled it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, just my personal thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T20:18:57-08:00","id":18909,"title":"","content":"I tend to assume (even if it's not canonical) that most sin-eater mementos have enough emotion and memory invested in them to count as Vestiges for mummies (seriously, any of the sample vestiges would be equally at home in the geist book). And also, that a lot of Uter and a few other relics are death-aspected enough to at least count as charms and possibly as memorabilia for sin-eater purposes. I like this because I really like mummy/sin-eater crossover, and having them chasing the same trinkets makes me happy. <br /> <br /> As for everyone else's magical gewgaws, none of them quite fit the mummy style, but vestiges are really thematically flexible, so I wouldn't find it totally ridiculous for a mummy to have a bunch of tokens chilling in their lifeweb, even if they aren't carrying them home to the judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T06:46:09-08:00","id":19146,"title":"","content":"AkD Relics: I tend to think of these as like gutter magic - a shorthand for collecting all the other gamelines' versions of supernatural gizmos into one category. What that means for Mummies is that they're case-by-case. (It would make a similar level of sense, be that great or small, for the Ascending Ones' Elixirs to be a distant descendant of Mummy's alchemy, with the poison-tolerance needed to use them a variant on the Guild tolerance to alchemical curses).<br /> <br /> Reliquary Relics: I tend to think of these as a more naturally occurring version of Mummy relics, and powered by Sekhem just the same. I'd say mummies can use/sacrifice them just fine. As they weren't made via the techniques developed in Irem, no guild has a specific talent for handling them, but they aren't usually powered by such severe curses, so that's rarely a problem.<br /> <br /> Sineater Mementos: Mementos are several different kinds of item. Charms and Memorabilia I'd suggest are the same as Reliquary relics, just death- rather than life-flavoured, and so mummies can at least sacrifice them. Vanitas and Fetters are too specialised to Sineaters' own powers, so I'd go with no. For Deathmasks, I'm undecided.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Fetishes: I'd go with no; they are rooted specifically in the magic of spirits and werewolves.<br /> <br /> Mage Artefacts: Maybe, but probably not. Supernal artefacts are highly symbolic, so mummies might be able to make some use of ones that are highly symbolic <i>of</i> things important to mummies - worship, civilisation, fate, the mummy's specific guild techniques. But Iremite magic is far more materialist than Supernal lore, and Artefacts might just seem empty of proper Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Mage Enhanced or Enchanted items: No.<br /> <br /> Changeling Tokens: I kind of think of glamour, from a human source, as dependent on that human's dSekhem/dt, but that's as close as they come. So I'd go with no.<br /> <br /> Since Vitriol was mentioned: Vitriol is, to my mind, a good candidate for being the same thing as Sekhem. Which might mean mummies can take it, though they'd need different techniques from lacuna. I think it should count as a memory sin though.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T09:04:24-08:00","id":19207,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that, of the example relics in the book, only about half of them seem to date back to irem. Given that mummies (who were the prime relic-makers in life) can't make relics anymore, it seems like relics <i>must</i> be the sort of thing that can happen in a generic way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-27T21:34:14-08:00","id":19541,"title":"","content":"Extremely gifted human beings (some of whom might be called &quot;sorcerers,&quot; but do *not* necessarily have a load of spells to toss at people) can create relics. Otherwise, the Storyteller determines if an item counts as a Sekhem-channeling object. Generally speaking, valid relics have curses that can only be avoided with Arisen guild initiation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T02:59:34-08:00","id":20576,"title":"","content":"<b>Activate Relic Item (Prime 2 Life 2 or Death 2)</b><br /> The willworker gains the ability to activate a Relic artificially satisfiying the trigger for such item.<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Compelling<br /> <b>Action:</b>Istant<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Prolonged (one scene)<br /> <b>Aspect: </b>Covert<br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b>Potency<br /> <b>Rote pool:</b>Intelligence + Occult + Prime<br /> The mage can activate the item\u2019s trigger at will anytime within this spell\u2019s Duration. See the Merit descriptions for Relics for more information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T19:25:17-08:00","id":21404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=19541#post19541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extremely gifted human beings (some of whom might be called &quot;sorcerers,&quot; but do *not* necessarily have a load of spells to toss at people) can create relics. Otherwise, the Storyteller determines if an item counts as a Sekhem-channeling object. Generally speaking, valid relics have curses that can only be avoided with Arisen guild initiation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got the feeling the fellas who have created relics over the years are the same kind of blokes who become demiurges for Prometheans. They have some combination of Obsession and Genius.<br /> <br /> I also feel like Leonardo Devinci would have made relics, if he wasn't some sort of enlightened supernatural being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-12T14:49:48-07:00","id":134387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=21404#post21404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got the feeling the fellas who have created relics over the years are the same kind of blokes who become demiurges for Prometheans. They have some combination of Obsession and Genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>This doesn't come with developmental authority but I don't think you're far off, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T16:43:05-07:00","id":615712,"title":"","content":"Excuse me while I perform the Rite of Return on this here thread...<br /> <br /> Anyway, my take on the subject goes something like this. Some forms of &quot;magic items&quot; are made with energies draw from human emotion or something similar. Fairy tokens certainly are, and while not all spirits are created by emotions alone the essence of the Shadow acts largely an &quot;echo&quot; of the real world. As such I say treat these as vestiges whenever a mummy tries to drain them. Mage artifacts and demonics Gadgets come from a sort of higher plane in terms of their power. Since Sekhem is supposed to come from the Gods and is subsequently shaped by human works (after a fashion) I would treat them as Relics for the purposes of draining. They can be part of a Lifeweb, but in terms of drawing upon their strength I'd say the &quot;Sekhem&quot; has been twisted too much (&quot;these lines of fate have been unwound and stitched into something alien and impure....&quot; or something). Under normal circumstances a mummy or a cultist cannot use it (unless it has an alternate method of use, like a Token's catch). For similar reasons I'd say a Mummy can only gain half the amount of Sekhem or Pillars from a given item (rounded up) . Sekhem flows through everything, and the resonance of Fate means it will pool in any mystical item. But an imperfect vessel intended to channel other forms of energy cannot contain the full power of Irem's ancient magics, and therefore yields less to a Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:53:56-07:00","id":615964,"title":"","content":"Where did you get the idea that sekhem comes from the gods? Sekhem comes from here, life itself, and is sent to the judges, not the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:15:23-07:00","id":616042,"title":"","content":"Indeed, according to the preview of the Egypt chapter of <i>To the Strongest</i> in Dark Eras, Sekhem is explicitly tied to the physical world. It has no particular connection to the Supernal Realms or any of the setting's other otherworlds, except for Duat and possibly the Underworld (which are, as I recall, explicitly <i>not</i> the same place). Since the Supernal Realms contain symbols for everything, Mages explicitly <i>can</i> create spells that interact with Sekhem, but it's known for being dangerous and difficult to control, and the Awakened are nowhere near as adept at manipulating it as the Shan'iatu were.<br /> <br /> Based on that, I'd say that Artifacts from Mage do <i>not</i> contain Sekhem, but that a sufficiently dedicated Mage could probably learn to make at least minor Relics. That said, the process of forcing Sekhem into a particular configuration should be a difficult and dangerous process, and by no means should it be possible for a Mage to start casually manufacturing relics to help a mummy friend out.<br /> <br /> As for tokens and the like, I'd say that anything from Arcadia or the Hedge contains no Sekhem and would probably be somewhat baffling to a mummy who came across it. Likewise, spirits don't seem to feed on or be a source of Sekhem, so Fetishes would be pretty much useless to mummies.<br /> <br /> With AKD and Reliquary Relics, I absolutely agree with Sunless Nick that they should be dealt with on a case-by-case basis. The Aegis Kai Doru doesn't seem to be very picky when it comes to the items they collect, and Spirit Slayers, at least, suggests they even stockpile things that they can't actually use. An AKD relic could be almost anything and have almost any kind of origin, but a fair number of them are probably Sekhem-bearing Relics created by mortals, either deliberately or (probably more often) by some freak combination of genius and providence.<br /> <br /> I don't know much about gadgets, but based on the description in the <i>God Machine Chronicle</i>, the God Machine seems to be pretty opportunistic about the occult resources it draws on to advance its agenda(s). I'd guess that its at least <i>aware</i> of Sekhem, and it's possible that it's made use of the energy in some capacity, so it may well be another case where items should be judged on an individual basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-05-2015, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:54:46-07:00","id":616471,"title":"","content":"Catdoom, gadgets and the god-machine aren't actually directly tied, it's more a kevin bacon thing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The God-Machine makes infrastructure, powered by Essence, which has some similarities to sekhem (it can be produced by sacrifice, especially human sacrifice). Could the god-machine make some infrastructure that could interact with Sekhem? I don't see any reason why not, really. <br /> <br /> Gadgets are made by demons though, and are powered by what is the equivalent of God-Machine Essence waste energy, so I can't see any connection to sekhem there. Heck, demons don't even have souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:13:33-07:00","id":616556,"title":"","content":"Fair enough; like I said, I don't really know anything about gadgets.<br /> <br /> As for the relationship between Essence and Sekhem, they strike me as <i>very</i> different things. Essence is an ephemeral product of emotions, actions, and events taking place in the physical world - a fear spirit feeds on the essence produced when people (and possibly animals) experience fear, while a car spirit feeds on the essence produced when a car is driven. Werewolves can gain essence by eating the flesh of humans or wolves, but I suspect that the essence comes from the <i>act</i> of eating and the emotions experienced by the prey, rather than being something present in the flesh itself. Likewise with human sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Sekhem, on the other hand, appears to be a sort of life-energy that suffuses the physical world. Unlike essence, it's <i>physical</i>, albeit invisible, and, when concentrated, can even by detected and measured by currently existing scientific tools. Where it comes from, exactly, is something of a mystery, but living things don't seem to generate it; they're suffused with it, and when they die it is released and (at least in some cases) sinks into Duat. If I were to compare it to anything, it actually seems conceptually most similar to vitae, and It's tempting to suggest that vitae is actually a specialized form of Sekhem that vampires and the strix are able to &quot;digest.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T18:23:00-07:00","id":617001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=615964#post615964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Where did you get the idea that sekhem comes from the gods? Sekhem comes from here, life itself, and is sent to the judges, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The gods created life and the world. And traditional Egyptian mythology describes the universe based on the ebb of the Nile- lifeforce, like the Inundation, is seen as a blessing from the gods that is given and renewed regularly for the living. Many myths portray one god or another breathing life into mortal bodies. The myth of the Aten goes even further and portrays the light of the Sun as a daily revitalization of all living things. Some said that lifeforce literally flows into the body as you draw in a breath, and leaves with every exhale. Credit for all of this- the wind, the Nile, and the rising of the Sun...this is all credited directly to the Gods. Sekhem isn't like Glamour or Essence. It reverberates through the living, sure. Also, through the stars and the Earth and geomantic patterns. It isn't emanating from living beings, though. Its more moving through them and between them, cycling endlessly between the real world and wherever Duat is in the cosmic scheme of things.<br /> <br /> That's my metaplot answer. My out of game answer is that magic items are really kinda a Mummy's &quot;thing&quot;. Vampires dance there way through social encounters, enslaving the minds of mortals with ease. Mages unlock secrets with preternatural sights and reshape magic in a thousand tricky ways. Werewolves kick the crap out of their enemies. Changelings excel at the art of dreams and promises. So here we are with Mummies. Dealing with magical artifacts are basically what they are all about. But necessity, really. They literally depend on magical toys to return to life (okay, toys and sacrifices, but mostly toys). Their whole society, the secret clubs they hang out in, all of those are literally based around the creation and study of a particular sort of magical doohicky. These guys spent their entire lives getting schooled in the art of making objects of power, and have spent the majority of their several thousand years of unlife hunting down said creations. So I ask you...if there was EVER a time that a supernatural entity should be able to mess around with a magic item usually off limits to all but one specific category of supernatural....who would that be? Okay, yes, probably Mages. But if there were TWO who should be able to do that, I defy you to say the second one isn't a goddamn Mummy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T21:51:44-07:00","id":617137,"title":"","content":"It isn't a goddamn mummy. There, that was easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mummy's don't have interest in magic items in general, but in relics in particular. Items empowered by sekhem using the lost arts of the Nameless Empire.<br /> <br /> Now if you want a mummy character to study the magic items of other splats to look for similarities in technique, sure that sounds like an interesting character concept. <br /> <br /> But success is something I wouldn't come front loaded, it's something the character earns through their efforts. <br /> <br /> The mummy meets a tokenspinning hedgecrafter, as an example. Can the mummy teach the changeling something they can apply to token crafting? Can the changeling teach the mummy something to get around a mummy's inability to make relics? Success or fail, that's a story. <br /> <br /> A mummy seeing a token and getting a ping on their relic radar though? Cheap, and rocks the mummy's theological boat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T22:08:42-07:00","id":617143,"title":"","content":"The thing is, though, that mummies <i>aren't </i>interested in &quot;magical items&quot; in a general sense; in fact, their goals (or, rather, the goals imposed on them by the Judges) are very specific. Their job is to send Sekhem to Duat, and they do this by (from their own perspective) reclaiming the works of lost Irem and those crafted by later people using the stolen secrets of the Nameless Empire. Artifacts, fetishes, tokens, and the like don't concern them, because they're only superficially similar to the relics they're actually interested in.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, &quot;magic item&quot; is a pretty arbitrary category. Artifacts, fetishes, and relics are all inanimate objects that have useful supernatural properties, but each type of item has an independent origin and operates according to different principals. Saying that mummies are interested in magic items is like saying that astronomers are interested in things which produce visible light, and suggesting that they therefore probably know as much about lighting fixtures and bioluminescence as they do about stars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-06-2015, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T18:12:02-07:00","id":618262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=616042#post616042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, according to the preview of the Egypt chapter of <i>To the Strongest</i> in Dark Eras, Sekhem is explicitly tied to the physical world. It has no particular connection to the Supernal Realms or any of the setting's other otherworlds, except for Duat and possibly the Underworld (which are, as I recall, explicitly <i>not</i> the same place).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't believe they ever explicitly called them out as separate or the same. I personally think Duat's under the Ocean of Fragments, but that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:08:09-07:00","id":618310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=618262#post618262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't believe they ever explicitly called them out as separate or the same. I personally think Duat's under the Ocean of Fragments, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I subscribe to that theory myself, but boy do I love how much sense it makes. Especially alongside the idea that Ammut is the cause of the Underworld's &quot;gravity&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T19:29:53-07:00","id":618318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=618262#post618262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't believe they ever explicitly called them out as separate or the same. I personally think Duat's under the Ocean of Fragments, but that's just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure it's been explicitly said that Duat isn't in the Underworld and is an entirely separate Lower Depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T20:12:29-07:00","id":618359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=618318#post618318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure it's been explicitly said that Duat isn't in the Underworld and is an entirely separate Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, it is entirely possible that the difference between the Underworld and a Lower Depth become a bit blurry if you go low enough. Sheol, the place where the Helminth in the book Summoners come from, is also a Lower Depth in all but name, and seemingly well connected to the (deep) Underworld. It is entirely possible that (part of) the deep Underworld has Irisses to Duat or even stranger places, or is at least metaphysically close to it, which probably makes opening new Irisses easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:03:00-07:00","id":619735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=617143#post617143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, though, that mummies <i>aren't </i>interested in &quot;magical items&quot; in a general sense; in fact, their goals (or, rather, the goals imposed on them by the Judges) are very specific. Their job is to send Sekhem to Duat, and they do this by (from their own perspective) reclaiming the works of lost Irem and those crafted by later people using the stolen secrets of the Nameless Empire. Artifacts, fetishes, tokens, and the like don't concern them, because they're only superficially similar to the relics they're actually interested in.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, &quot;magic item&quot; is a pretty arbitrary category. Artifacts, fetishes, and relics are all inanimate objects that have useful supernatural properties, but each type of item has an independent origin and operates according to different principals. Saying that mummies are interested in magic items is like saying that astronomers are interested in things which produce visible light, and suggesting that they therefore probably know as much about lighting fixtures and bioluminescence as they do about stars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 'Those crafted by later people using the stolen secrets of the Nameless Empire', huh? I don't think that even holds up given the items in the core book specifically identified as Relics. Sure, some are from Irem, and some maybe could have been from some unknown splinter of Irem lore....but definitely not every last item. The Keening Box of Karl Von Becker has a specific origin that doesn't involve Irem or Egyptian folklore, for example. There also an Effigy of a toy car that seems to have had Sekhem latch onto it as a result of trauma and fate rather than design. The playing field is simply wider than you say it is. I say no harm in making it wider still. Sekhem favors first the reanimated bodies of the Arisem, second Relics designed (often deliberately, sometimes by coincidence) to house that magic, and finally other items of power. Remember that Sekhem doesn't just lie dormant in an object. It flows. The LIfeweb is an obvious manifestation of this. Less seen is the way Sekhem flows between the living, passing in and out like a breath. So too can it flow into and out architecture. That was the whole point of Irem's geomantic pillars. So, what reason is there to say it does not flow through more unique objects of power? Indeed, I would say any such object by its very nature creates permutations in Fate (after all, whatever its intended effect is going to have some impact on reality, big or small, and thus will shift the tides of Fate in the aftermath). Sekhem is drawn to such things like iron to a magnet.<br /> <br /> Look, at the end of the day we will all play the game our own way. For me personally, I look at all those WOD books teeming with their various magical items and I can almost hear them whisper &quot;Hey,I'm a potential adventure waiting to happen!&quot; And for my part, if I see a great adventure waiting to happen I'm not going to be discouraged from telling it just because some uppity wizard or wolf thinks it should stay in their little clubhouse. Doubly so because its a simple window into crossover stories if the ST is in need of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T21:04:11-07:00","id":619736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=618318#post618318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure it's been explicitly said that Duat isn't in the Underworld and is an entirely separate Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do you remember where? I'm drawing a complete blank over any supplement making that explicit a statement about the nature of the Judge's Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T12:39:38-07:00","id":620393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/18885-mummy-and-magical-items-from-other-supernaturals?p=619735#post619735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 'Those crafted by later people using the stolen secrets of the Nameless Empire', huh? I don't think that even holds up given the items in the core book specifically identified as Relics. Sure, some are from Irem, and some maybe could have been from some unknown splinter of Irem lore....but definitely not every last item. The Keening Box of Karl Von Becker has a specific origin that doesn't involve Irem or Egyptian folklore, for example. There also an Effigy of a toy car that seems to have had Sekhem latch onto it as a result of trauma and fate rather than design. The playing field is simply wider than you say it is. I say no harm in making it wider still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm well aware that not every relic is literally built on the secrets of Irem (though the most potent ones tend to be), but that seems to be what the Arisen <i>believe</i>. They tend to have a pretty narrow and warped world view, which tells them that all human civilizations are inheritors of Irem's lore and imitators of its glory. <i>All</i> human crafts were originated or perfected in Irem, and as far as they're concerned that means that all man-made objects that are genius enough in their construction to channel Sekhem are the rightful property of the Judges.<br /> <br /> Their definition of a &quot;relic&quot; <i>is</i> therefore quite broad, but it is also fairly specific. Relics are products of human artifice and are powered by Sekhem. If an object doesn't meet those two qualifications, then it isn't a relic. Vestiges, on the other hand, are often created by chance, and I would generally agree with the idea that some or all of the momentos prized by Sin Eaters would also qualify as vestiges. As for the toy car effigy, it's something of an exceptional case, and it's noteworthy that it's creation involved what might arguably be called a human sacrifice, and that a Mummy was present and using its powers at the time, so Sekhem was probably flowing through the area in more than the usual quantities.<br /> <br /> But you are, of course, correct that anybody can run the game any way that they like. I personally don't really see the need for Mummies to pursue the magical items used by other splats - genuine relics don't seem to be <i>that</i> rare in any case, and they're unique in that pretty much anyone can use many of them - but if you disagree that's fine. Having Mummies go after artifacts and fetishes in the like <i>would</i> obviously be a good way to build conflict between them and the other supernatural beings in the setting, so I could see it being an attractive option if that's the kind of game you want to run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 08-08-2015, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}